  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, showing a large ~9% jump over single-profile multimodal (config_016, 0.527). This confirms multi-profile aggregation is the most impactful design axis. However, we have only tested avgpool aggregation in the multi-profile setting; transformer aggregation is completely untested and could allow the model to learn profile-specific attention weights rather than uniform averaging. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool for combining multiple profiles in the multimodal setting? This is a clean one-variable change from the current best (config_018 → config_020: avgpool → transformer, everything else identical). Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, testing the aggregation mechanism in the already-validated multi-profile multimodal regime directly targets the largest remaining uncertainty in the most promising architecture. A positive result would identify a new best configuration; a null/negative result would confirm avgpool sufficiency and redirect budget toward other axes (e.g., image encoder quality via ViT-L). Either outcome significantly reduces uncertainty about a core architectural decision."
}

